+# 0493x9i — prescribed contact angle on the generic x9h wall provider
+
+Incremental patch on top of **0493x9h**.  x9g remains the A/B phase-pair
+abstraction and x9h remains the mechanism-independent wall geometry provider.
+x9i adds the first wetting closure without changing physical x6c alpha, the x6f
+interface location, the Q6 CG solve, B1, streaming, collision, thermostat or
+resampling.
+
+## Physical convention
+
+New parameter:
+
+```text
+phaseInterfaceContactAngleDegrees = -1
+```
+
+`-1` disables wetting and preserves the qualified free-interface path.  Values
+in `[0,180]` activate a prescribed static angle measured **through phase A**.
+
+The two capillary phases remain A and B, e.g.
+
+```text
+phaseInterfaceASelector = type:1
+phaseInterfaceBSelector = type:2
+```
+
+The wall is a third geometry provider.  Therefore an active contact angle does
+**not** use `phaseInterfaceBSelector=wall`.  `B=wall` remains the passive x9h
+geometry-only mode.
+
+With the existing orientation conventions
+
+- `nAB`: A -> B (`-grad(alphaA)`),
+- `nWall`: fluid -> solid (`grad(solidFraction)`),
+
+x9i enforces
+
+```text
+nAB . nWall = -cos(thetaA)
+```
+
+in the wall/interface contact band.
+
+## Numerical closure
+
+The production capillary chain remains
+
+```text
+physical alpha_x6c
+  -> curvature-only p3 alphaK
+  -> Scharr nAB(raw)
+  -> x9i wall/contact-band normal replacement
+  -> Scharr div(nAB)
+  -> kappa
+  -> sigma*kappa
+  -> phiGamma
+```
+
+Only the p3 normal is modified.  `alpha_x6c` and the x6f `alpha=0.5` geometry
+are untouched.
+
+A cell is eligible when
+
+1. the x9h wall normal is valid;
+2. a 3x3 neighbourhood of physical x6c alpha brackets `0.5`;
+3. the raw p3 phase normal is valid.
+
+For a unit wall tangent `t=(-nWall_y,nWall_x)`, the tangent sign is taken from
+the raw A->B normal to preserve the local interface orientation, then
+
+```text
+d = -cos(thetaA)
+s = sign(nRaw . t)
+nAB = d*nWall + s*sqrt(1-d*d)*t
+```
+
+is written back to the production p3 normal field.
+
+## Wall source
+
+x9i requests exactly the x9h provider.  It therefore works with
+
+- static domain walls (`solid`, `specular`, `bounceback` geometry), and
+- a Darcy/chi geometry only when the existing
+  `darcyChiCollisionVpEnable=true` declaration says that chi represents wall
+  geometry.
+
+No generic porous Darcy field is silently converted into a wetting wall.
+
+## Diagnostics
+
+New summary-cadence file:
+
+```text
+output/cuda_contact_angle_0493x9i.csv
+```
+
+It reports the prescribed angle, target dot product, candidate/corrected cell
+counts, raw and corrected mean angles, closure RMS errors, and contact-band
+curvature statistics.
+
+The angle/dot closure is a hard structural validation.  Contact-band curvature
+is printed as information in x9i: detailed wall-curvature bias and sessile-drop
+equilibrium belong to the subsequent physical qualification.
+
+## Qualification runner
+
+`run_0493x9i_contact_angle.sh` generates circular sessile caps at 60, 90 and
+120 degrees.  For a bottom wall at `y=0`, a circle of radius `R` with
+
+```text
+yCenter = -R*cos(theta)
+```
+
+has the requested contact angle through A and exact free-interface curvature
+`1/R`.
+
+Default campaign is deliberately short (`STEPS=1`): it qualifies the initial
+geometry/closure before dynamic relaxation can obscure the wall reconstruction.
+LiveVis is ON and filtered recording is OFF by default.
+
+## Apply
+
+From repository root after extracting the bundle:
+
+```bash
+python3 x9i_bundle/tools/apply_0493x9i_contact_angle.py
+bash -n scripts/run_0493x9i_contact_angle.sh
+python3 -m py_compile \
+  scripts/generate_0493x9i_sessile_cap_state.py \
+  scripts/analyze_0493x9i_contact_angle.py
+g++ -std=c++17 -Iinclude -fsyntax-only src/params_io_base.cpp
+bash scripts/build_src_mpcd_cuda_q6_resident_livevis_0486.sh
+```
+
+The installer is semantic/idempotent and does not impose a Git working-tree
+guard.
+
